// Code-signing overrides for CI only. Applied via xcodebuild's documented
// XCODE_XCCONFIG_FILE environment variable, which layers this on top of the
// project's own configuration without modifying it — so a developer's local
// build and a real signed release are completely unaffected by this file.
//
// Why it is needed: macos/Runner.xcodeproj pins the Release configuration to
// CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual with DEVELOPMENT_TEAM 3UC8WFTV3Y and an
// "Apple Development" identity. A GitHub-hosted runner has no keychain, no
// certificate and no provisioning profile, so the build died with:
//
//   error: No profiles for 'com.voltx.voltxMobile' were found: Xcode couldn't
//   find any Mac App Development provisioning profiles matching
//   'com.voltx.voltxMobile'.
//
// Signing is a distribution concern, not a correctness one. Everything CI is
// actually checking — that the Dart, the plugins and the native Runner target
// all compile and link for release — still runs in full. The only thing
// skipped is attaching a signature the runner could not produce anyway.
//
// Do NOT include this file in a build that is meant to be distributed: the
// resulting .app is unsigned and will be refused by Gatekeeper.

CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY =
CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS =
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED = NO
CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = NO
DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =
PROVISIONING_PROFILE_SPECIFIER =
